---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import PageHero from "../../components/PageHero.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy & Terms"
  description="The Jentosy Project's privacy policy and terms of use."
>
  <PageHero eyebrow="Legal" heading="Privacy & Terms" />

  <section class="on-light section">
    <div class="container narrow">
      <p class="effective-date">Effective date: August 26, 2026</p>

      <h2 class="h3">Privacy Policy</h2>
      <p>
        The Jentosy Project, Inc. ("The Jentosy Project," "we," "us") collects only the
        information needed to process donations, respond to inquiries and partnership requests,
        and understand how visitors use this site.
      </p>
      <p><strong>Information we collect</strong></p>
      <ul class="check-list">
        <li>Contact details you submit through our Contact, Partner With Us, or newsletter forms — name, email address, organization, and message content.</li>
        <li>Donation information processed on our behalf by Zeffy, our third-party donation platform — see below.</li>
        <li>Aggregate, anonymized site-usage data collected via Google Analytics (pages visited, general location, device type) — never tied back to your name or email by us.</li>
      </ul>
      <p><strong>How we use it</strong></p>
      <p>
        We use the information you provide to respond to your message, process your donation and
        send a receipt, send occasional updates if you've opted in, and understand which parts of
        the site are useful to visitors. We do not sell, rent, or trade your personal information
        to any third party for marketing purposes.
      </p>
      <p><strong>Donation processing</strong></p>
      <p>
        Donations made through this site are processed and held by <strong>Zeffy</strong>, an
        independent donation platform — not by The Jentosy Project directly. Zeffy handles your
        payment card details under its own privacy policy and security practices; we receive your
        name, email, and donation amount so we can issue a receipt and keep you informed.
      </p>
      <p><strong>Cookies &amp; analytics</strong></p>
      <p>
        This site uses Google Analytics (GA4) to understand aggregate visitor behavior. Google
        Analytics uses cookies and similar technologies; you can opt out using your browser
        settings or a browser extension such as Google's Analytics Opt-out add-on. We do not use
        advertising or cross-site tracking cookies.
      </p>
      <p><strong>Your choices</strong></p>
      <p>
        You can ask us to correct or delete the personal information we hold about you, and you
        can unsubscribe from any email update at any time using the link in that email or by{" "}
        <a href="/contact/">contacting us directly</a>. We will not use your information for any
        purpose beyond what's described here without asking you first.
      </p>

      <h2 class="h3">Donor Disclosures</h2>
      <p>
        The Jentosy Project, Inc. is a 501(c)(3) public charity. Donations are tax-deductible to
        the extent allowed by law, and no goods or services were provided in exchange for your
        gift unless stated otherwise at the time of donation. You will receive an automated,
        tax-compliant receipt by email for every donation, one-time or recurring.
      </p>
      <p>
        Recurring monthly donations can be modified or canceled at any time through the link in
        your Zeffy receipt email, or by <a href="/contact/">contacting us</a> and we will process
        the change promptly. Donations are non-refundable except where required by law; if you
        believe a donation was made in error, contact us and we'll work with you directly.
      </p>

      <h2 class="h3">Terms of Use</h2>
      <p>
        By using this site, you agree to the following terms. If you don't agree, please don't
        use the site.
      </p>
      <p><strong>Medical content</strong></p>
      <p>
        Content on this site about FSGS, APOL1-mediated kidney disease, and chronic kidney
        disease generally is provided for general educational purposes only and is{" "}
        <strong>not medical advice</strong>. It does not create a doctor-patient relationship and
        should never replace guidance from a qualified healthcare provider. Always consult your
        doctor or a nephrologist about your own diagnosis, testing, or treatment. This educational
        content has not yet completed a formal clinical-accuracy review — see the note on each
        disease page for details.
      </p>
      <p><strong>Intellectual property</strong></p>
      <p>
        Text, illustrations, and data visualizations on this site are the property of The Jentosy
        Project, Inc. unless otherwise credited, and may not be reproduced for commercial purposes
        without permission. Cited statistics remain the property of their original sources (CDC,
        USRDS, NIDDK, and the peer-reviewed studies linked throughout the site).
      </p>
      <p><strong>No warranty</strong></p>
      <p>
        This site is provided "as is." While we work to keep information accurate and sourced, The
        Jentosy Project makes no warranty as to completeness or fitness for any particular purpose,
        and is not liable for decisions made based on this site's content.
      </p>
      <p><strong>Contact</strong></p>
      <p>
        Questions about this policy or your information can be sent through our{" "}
        <a href="/contact/">Contact page</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .narrow {
    max-width: 680px;
  }

  .effective-date {
    font-size: 12.5px;
    color: var(--fg-muted);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-6);
  }

  .check-list li {
    max-width: none;
  }
</style>
